steps.body:
A grid arrives as lines of characters. Split the input into lines, then split each line into single characters so you can write `grid[r][c]`.

```stdin
##..
#..#
...#
```

```javascript harness
const input = require("fs").readFileSync(0, "utf8");
const rows = 3;
const cols = 4;
{{code}}
console.log(grid.map((row) => row.join("")).join("\n"));
console.log(`visited: ${visited.length} rows of ${visited[0].length}`);
```

```javascript
const grid = input.trim().split("\n").map((line) => line.trim().split(""));
const directions = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]]; // down, up, right, left
const visited = Array.from({ length: rows }, () => new Array(cols).fill(false));
```

Depth-first search (DFS) goes as deep as it can before it backs up. From a cell, try each direction offset. **Check the bounds first**: `grid[-1]` is `undefined`, and reading `grid[-1][c]` throws a TypeError. Then skip cells that are visited or not part of the region.

Mark a cell visited *before* you explore its neighbors, or two neighbors keep calling each other until the call stack overflows. Keep visited in a boolean grid built with `Array.from`, so every row is its own array. A Set of `[r, c]` arrays never matches a new `[r, c]` array.

To count regions, loop over every cell and start a DFS from each unvisited one that belongs to a region. Each start is a new region, and the size the DFS returns is that region's size.

Each recursive call adds a frame to the call stack, so keep recursive grid searches to about 50 by 50.

example.code:
const input = require("fs").readFileSync(0, "utf8");
const grid = input.trim().split("\n").map((line) => line.trim().split(""));
const rows = grid.length;
const cols = grid[0].length;
const directions = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]];
const visited = Array.from({ length: rows }, () => new Array(cols).fill(false));

function islandSize(r, c) {
  visited[r][c] = true;
  let size = 1;
  for (const [dr, dc] of directions) {
    const nr = r + dr;
    const nc = c + dc;
    if (nr < 0 || nr >= rows || nc < 0 || nc >= cols) {
      continue;
    }
    if (!visited[nr][nc] && grid[nr][nc] === "#") {
      size += islandSize(nr, nc);
    }
  }
  return size;
}

const sizes = [];
for (let r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
  for (let c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
    if (grid[r][c] === "#" && !visited[r][c]) {
      sizes.push(islandSize(r, c));
    }
  }
}
console.log(`Islands: ${sizes.length}`);
console.log(`Sizes: ${sizes.join(", ")}`);

